From 211ad871cbd3fb44dec0c75c69b0d9132f644072 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:02:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ipa: simple: add contrast detection auto focus

The simple pipeline had no lens support. Gather a sharpness measure in
the software ISP statistics (sum of absolute differences of horizontally
neighbouring green samples over the centre of the image, with the green
sum to normalise it), add an Af algorithm that sweeps the lens coarsely,
then finely around the peak, and in continuous mode starts over when
sharpness or brightness changes for a while.

The pipeline hands the lens position control to the IPA along with the
sensor controls, applies it to the focus lens, and parks the lens when
the camera stops (a voice coil holding a position draws current).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
